<h1>Log Review — Credentials &amp; PII</h1>
<div class="date">Internal note · November 2026</div>

<p>
  This note records the log review I carried out to find credentials and personal
  data that had been written into our logs. Logs were pulled from CloudWatch and
  searched for anything sensitive, so that exposed secrets could be rotated and any
  exposed personal data cleaned up at source.
</p>

<h2>Scope</h2>
<p>In scope:</p>
<ul>
  <li>CloudWatch log groups for the in-scope ECS clusters and infrastructure hosts.</li>
  <li>The last 31 days of events per log group.</li>
  <li>Spring Boot / Java applications and infrastructure services — PostgreSQL, nginx,
      Squid, Postfix, Dovecot, OpenLDAP, ActiveMQ, Grafana, Prometheus, pgAdmin,
      JasperReports and WireMock.</li>
  <li>Shell command history where it appears in those logs.</li>
</ul>
<p>Not in scope: live systems and configuration files that are not shipped to
  CloudWatch, and anything outside the listed log groups and 31-day window.</p>

<h2>Credentials searched for</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Example keywords</th><th>Severity</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Generic password / secret</td><td>Passwords and secrets assigned a value</td><td><code>password=</code>, <code>secret=</code>, <code>passphrase</code></td><td>High</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Inline env secret</td><td>Secrets set as environment variables</td><td><code>PGPASSWORD=</code>, <code>MYSQL_PWD=</code>, <code>*_PASSWORD=</code>, <code>*_TOKEN=</code></td><td>High</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mail (SASL)</td><td>Postfix / Dovecot auth and SMTP AUTH blobs</td><td><code>sasl_password=</code>, <code>AUTH PLAIN</code>, <code>AUTH LOGIN</code></td><td>Critical</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Proxy / HTTP auth</td><td>Squid and HTTP basic / bearer headers</td><td><code>Proxy-Authorization</code>, <code>Authorization: Basic</code>, <code>Bearer</code></td><td>High</td></tr>
    <tr><td>URL / JDBC credentials</td><td>Credentials inside a connection string</td><td><code>scheme://user:pass@</code>, <code>jdbc:…?password=</code></td><td>Critical</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Spring Boot / Java</td><td>Framework config and JVM secrets</td><td><code>spring.datasource.password</code>, <code>-Djavax.net.ssl.*Password</code>, <code>client-secret</code></td><td>Critical</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Password hashes</td><td>Hashes written to logs</td><td><code>$apr1$</code>, <code>$6$</code>, <code>{SSHA}</code></td><td>Medium</td></tr>
    <tr><td>OpenLDAP</td><td>Directory root / bind credentials</td><td><code>rootpw</code>, <code>olcRootPW</code>, <code>bindpw</code></td><td>Critical</td></tr>
    <tr><td>SNMP</td><td>Community strings</td><td><code>community</code>, <code>rocommunity</code></td><td>High</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Private keys</td><td>PEM private key material</td><td><code>-----BEGIN … PRIVATE KEY-----</code></td><td>Critical</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CLI / shell history</td><td>Secrets passed on the command line</td><td><code>mysql -p…</code>, <code>curl -u user:pass</code>, <code>redis-cli -a</code></td><td>High</td></tr>
    <tr><td>App services</td><td>Service-specific secrets</td><td>Grafana <code>admin_password</code> / tokens, Prometheus <code>bearer_token</code>, pgAdmin / WireMock passwords</td><td>High</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Personal data searched for</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>What it covers</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Biometric references</td><td>Mentions of biometric handling</td><td><code>voiceprint</code>, <code>palmprint</code>, <code>faceID</code>, <code>minutiae</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Format / standard markers</td><td>Biometric interchange formats</td><td><code>.wsq</code>, <code>ISO 19794</code>, <code>NIST-ITL</code>, <code>CBEFF</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Email address</td><td>Personal / user email addresses</td><td><code>name@domain.tld</code></td></tr>
    <tr><td>Date of birth</td><td>DOB values (labelled)</td><td><code>dob=</code>, <code>date_of_birth:</code></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>What the patterns mean</h2>
<p>Each category is a keyword plus a regular expression matching the value's shape. A few of the main ones:</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Inline environment secrets</b> — secrets set as an env variable on a logged command line: <code>PGPASSWORD=</code>, <code>MYSQL_PWD=</code>, <code>*_PASSWORD=</code>, <code>*_TOKEN=</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Generic key/value secrets</b> — any secret-named field with a value: <code>password</code>, <code>secret</code>, <code>token</code> followed by <code>:</code> or <code>=</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Embedded-credential URLs</b> — <code>scheme://user:pass@host</code> and JDBC URLs carrying a password.</li>
  <li><b>Password hashes</b> — <code>$apr1$</code>, <code>$6$</code> (crypt) and <code>{SSHA}</code> (LDAP / Dovecot).</li>
  <li><b>Shell-history credentials</b> — secrets given as command arguments: <code>mysql -p</code>, <code>curl -u</code>, <code>redis-cli -a</code>.</li>
  <li><b>Biometric / biographic</b> — biometric field references and formats, email addresses, and labelled date-of-birth fields.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How the search was done</h2>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Collect</td><td>31 days of events downloaded per log group from CloudWatch with the AWS CLI.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Chunk</td><td>Large logs split into smaller pieces so nothing is skipped for size.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Scan</td><td>Each piece scanned with Trivy against the credential and PII pattern sets.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Triage</td><td>Findings deduplicated and ranked; low-signal noise set aside.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Validate</td><td>Each real finding read back from the source log to confirm it is a genuine exposure before rotation.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>
  The scanning was done with <b>Trivy</b>, an open-source scanner from Aqua Security used for
  vulnerability, misconfiguration and secret scanning. Its secret scanner matches file content against
  rules, each a keyword plus a regular expression. Trivy's built-in rules target cloud / SaaS tokens, so
  for our infrastructure and application secrets I supplied custom rule sets.
</p>

<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Trivy secret scanner</td><td>Matches log content against the rules (<code>trivy fs --scanners secret</code>).</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Custom credential rules</td><td>Define the credential categories above, passed with <code>--secret-config</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Custom PII rules</td><td>Define the biometric and biographic categories, run as a separate pass.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Collection &amp; chunking</td><td>AWS CLI downloader plus splitting of oversized logs.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Triage / reveal</td><td>Aggregates results, removes duplicates, and shows the real value of each confirmed finding.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>


<h2>Credential rules used (trivy-secret.yaml)</h2>
<pre class="yaml"><code># trivy-secret.yaml
# Custom Trivy secret-scanning rules ported from scan-ecs-logs-for-credentials.sh
# so Trivy catches the INFRA-service and Spring Boot/Java credentials that its
# built-in rules (tuned for cloud/SaaS tokens) do not.
#
# Use:  trivy fs --scanners secret --secret-config trivy-secret.yaml &lt;path&gt;
# (scan-logs-trivy.sh picks this file up automatically if it&#x27;s in the CWD.)
#
# These ADD to Trivy&#x27;s built-in rules; they don&#x27;t replace them.
# Each rule needs &gt;=1 keyword: Trivy only runs the regex on a file when a
# keyword is present, which keeps scanning fast. Regex is Go/RE2 syntax.

rules:
  # ---- generic ---------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-generic-password
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Generic password assignment
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;password&quot;, &quot;passwd&quot;, &quot;passphrase&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(password|passwd|pwd|passphrase)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-generic-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Generic secret / client secret
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;secret&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(client[_-]?secret|api[_-]?secret|secret)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-env-inline-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Inline env secret (PASSWORD/SECRET/TOKEN=)
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;PASSWORD&quot;, &quot;SECRET&quot;, &quot;TOKEN&quot;, &quot;PGPASSWORD&quot;, &quot;MYSQL_PWD&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)[a-z0-9_]*(password|secret|token)=\S+&#x27;

  # ---- mail (postfix / dovecot) ---------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-mail-sasl
    category: InfraCreds
    title: SASL username/password
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;sasl_&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)sasl_(username|password)\s*=\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-smtp-auth-blob
    category: InfraCreds
    title: SMTP AUTH PLAIN/LOGIN base64 blob
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;AUTH PLAIN&quot;, &quot;AUTH LOGIN&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;AUTH (PLAIN|LOGIN)\s+[A-Za-z0-9+/=]{8,}&#x27;

  # ---- proxy / http ----------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-squid-proxy-auth
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Proxy authorization
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;Proxy-Authorization&quot;, &quot;proxy_auth&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(proxy-authorization|proxy_auth)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-http-basic-auth
    category: InfraCreds
    title: HTTP Basic auth header
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;Basic&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)authorization:\s*basic\s+[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-bearer-token
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Bearer token
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;Bearer&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)authorization:\s*bearer\s+[A-Za-z0-9._-]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-jwt
    category: InfraCreds
    title: JWT (check exp)
    severity: MEDIUM
    keywords: [&quot;eyJ&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-url-embedded-cred
    category: InfraCreds
    title: URL with embedded user:pass
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;://&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*://[^/\s:@]+:[^/\s:@]+@&#x27;

  # ---- Spring Boot / Java ----------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-spring-datasource-pw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Spring datasource password
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;datasource.password&quot;, &quot;SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(spring\.datasource\.password|spring_datasource_password)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-spring-prop-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Spring property password/secret
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;spring.&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)spring\.[a-z0-9._-]*(password|secret)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-jdbc-url-query-cred
    category: InfraCreds
    title: JDBC URL with password/user in query
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;jdbc:&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)jdbc:[a-z0-9]+://\S*(password|passwd|user)=[^\s&amp;&quot;;]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-jdbc-url-userinfo
    category: InfraCreds
    title: JDBC URL with user:pass@ userinfo
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;jdbc:&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)jdbc:[a-z0-9]+://[^/\s:@]+:[^/\s:@]+@&#x27;

  - id: infra-keystore-password
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Java keystore/truststore password
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;storePassword&quot;, &quot;store-password&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(keystorepassword|truststorepassword|key-store-password|trust-store-password)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-java-ssl-dprop
    category: InfraCreds
    title: JVM -Djavax.net.ssl keystore/truststore password
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;javax.net.ssl&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)-Djavax\.net\.ssl\.(keyStore|trustStore)Password=\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-jvm-dprop-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: JVM -D system property secret
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;-D&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)-D[a-z0-9._]*(password|passwd|pwd|secret|token)=\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-kafka-jaas-pw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Kafka SASL JAAS config password
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;jaas.config&quot;, &quot;LoginModule&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(sasl\.jaas\.config|loginmodule).{0,80}?password\s*=\s*&quot;?[^\s&quot;]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-oauth-client-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: OAuth2 client secret
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;client-secret&quot;, &quot;client_secret&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)client[_-]secret\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  # ---- snmp / dns ------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-snmp-community
    category: InfraCreds
    title: SNMP community string
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;community&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(ro|rw)?community\s+\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-dns-tsig-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: BIND/TSIG secret
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;secret&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;secret\s+&quot;[A-Za-z0-9+/=]{8,}&quot;&#x27;

  # ---- hashes ----------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-hash-crypt
    category: InfraCreds
    title: crypt/apr1 password hash
    severity: MEDIUM
    keywords: [&quot;$apr1$&quot;, &quot;$6$&quot;, &quot;$5$&quot;, &quot;$1$&quot;, &quot;$2&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;\$(apr1|1|5|6|2[aby]?)\$[^\s]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-hash-ldap
    category: InfraCreds
    title: LDAP/dovecot SSHA hash
    severity: MEDIUM
    keywords: [&quot;{SSHA}&quot;, &quot;{SHA}&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)\{s?sha[0-9]*\}[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+&#x27;

  # ---- private keys ----------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-pem-private-key
    category: InfraCreds
    title: PEM private key header
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;PRIVATE KEY&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;-----BEGIN ([A-Z0-9]+ )?PRIVATE KEY-----&#x27;

  # ---- CLI / shell-history idioms -------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-cli-mysql-p
    category: InfraCreds
    title: mysql -p&lt;password&gt; on command line
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;mysql&quot;, &quot;mysqldump&quot;, &quot;mariadb&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(mysql|mysqldump|mariadb)\s[^#]*\s-p[^\s=]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-cli-curl-userpass
    category: InfraCreds
    title: curl -u user:pass
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;curl&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;curl\s.*(-u|--user)\s+\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-cli-redis-auth
    category: InfraCreds
    title: redis-cli -a &lt;password&gt;
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;redis-cli&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;redis-cli\s.*-a\s+\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-cli-htpasswd-b
    category: InfraCreds
    title: htpasswd -b user pass
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;htpasswd&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;htpasswd\s.*-b\s+\S+\s+\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-cli-doveadm-pw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: doveadm pw -p &lt;plaintext&gt;
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;doveadm&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;doveadm\s+pw\s.*-p\s+\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-cli-openssl-pass
    category: InfraCreds
    title: openssl pass:&lt;secret&gt;
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;pass:&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;pass:\S+&#x27;

  # ===========================================================================
  # Service-specific additions: postgres, nginx, openldap, pgadmin, grafana,
  # prometheus, jaspersoft, wiremock
  # ===========================================================================

  # ---- PostgreSQL ------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-postgres-uri
    category: InfraCreds
    title: PostgreSQL URI with embedded password
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;postgres://&quot;, &quot;postgresql://&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)postgres(ql)?://[^/\s:@]+:[^/\s:@]+@\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-postgres-conninfo-pw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: libpq conninfo password (password=... near host/dbname)
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;dbname&quot;, &quot;host=&quot;, &quot;hostaddr&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(password|pwd)\s*=\s*&#x27;&#x27;?[^&#x27;&#x27;\s]+&#x27;&#x27;?\s*(host|hostaddr|dbname|port|user)=&#x27;

  # ---- nginx -----------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-nginx-proxy-pass-cred
    category: InfraCreds
    title: nginx proxy_pass upstream with embedded creds
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;proxy_pass&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)proxy_pass\s+https?://[^/\s:@]+:[^/\s:@]+@&#x27;

  # ---- OpenLDAP --------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-ldap-rootpw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: OpenLDAP rootpw / olcRootPW
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;rootpw&quot;, &quot;olcRootPW&quot;]
    # require an actual value (hash / crypt / quoted / base64), so slapd MOD
    # logs that only NAME the attr=olcRootPW (value masked) don&#x27;t false-positive
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(olcrootpw|rootpw)\s*[:=]{0,2}\s*(\{(crypt|s?sha[0-9]*|s?md5|clear|plain|pbkdf2[a-z0-9]*)\}[^\s]+|\$[0-9a-z]+\$[^\s]+|&quot;[^&quot;]{4,}&quot;|[A-Za-z0-9+/]{12,}={0,2})&#x27;

  - id: infra-ldap-bindpw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: LDAP bind password (bindpw / bind_password)
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;bindpw&quot;, &quot;bind_password&quot;, &quot;bindpassword&quot;, &quot;bind-password&quot;]
    # value must be non-space AND non-asterisk, so masked &quot;bindpw ****&quot; and
    # bare attribute-name mentions don&#x27;t false-positive
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(bindpw|bind[_-]?password)\s*[:=]?\s*[^\s*]{3,}&#x27;

  - id: infra-ldap-cli-w
    category: InfraCreds
    title: ldap* -w &lt;password&gt; on command line
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;ldapsearch&quot;, &quot;ldapmodify&quot;, &quot;ldapadd&quot;, &quot;ldapwhoami&quot;, &quot;ldapdelete&quot;, &quot;ldappasswd&quot;, &quot;ldapcompare&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)ldap(search|modify|add|delete|whoami|compare|passwd|modrdn)\b.*\s-w\s+\S+&#x27;

  # ---- JSON-quoted creds (pgAdmin servers.json, Grafana provisioning, etc.) --
  - id: infra-json-quoted-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: JSON key password/secret/token with quoted value
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;password&quot;, &quot;secret&quot;, &quot;token&quot;, &quot;apikey&quot;, &quot;api_key&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)&quot;(password|passwd|secret|secret_key|token|api[_-]?key|basicAuthPassword)&quot;\s*:\s*&quot;[^&quot;]+&quot;&#x27;

  # ---- Grafana ---------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-grafana-admin-password
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Grafana admin password
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD&quot;, &quot;admin_password&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(GF_SECURITY_ADMIN_PASSWORD|admin_password)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-grafana-token
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Grafana API key / service-account token
    severity: CRITICAL
    keywords: [&quot;glsa_&quot;, &quot;glc_&quot;, &quot;eyJrIjoi&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(glsa_[A-Za-z0-9_]{8,}|glc_[A-Za-z0-9_=+/-]{8,}|eyJrIjoi[A-Za-z0-9/+=]+)&#x27;

  - id: infra-grafana-datasource-pw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Grafana datasource basicAuthPassword / secureJsonData
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;basicAuthPassword&quot;, &quot;secureJsonData&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(basicauthpassword|secureJsonData)[^\n]{0,40}?[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  # ---- Prometheus ------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-prometheus-bearer-token
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Prometheus bearer_token in scrape config
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;bearer_token&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)bearer_token\s*:\s*\S+&#x27;

  - id: infra-prometheus-credentials
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Prometheus authorization credentials
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;credentials&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)credentials\s*:\s*\S+&#x27;

  # ---- JasperReports / JasperSoft -------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-jasper-db-password
    category: InfraCreds
    title: JasperReports repository / datasource password
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;metadata.hibernate&quot;, &quot;repository.jdbc&quot;, &quot;jdbc.password&quot;, &quot;js.password&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(metadata\.hibernate\.password|repository\.jdbc\.password|jdbc\.password|js\.password)\s*[:=]\s*\S+&#x27;

  # ---- WireMock --------------------------------------------------------------
  - id: infra-wiremock-keystore-pw
    category: InfraCreds
    title: WireMock keystore / key-manager / truststore password
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;keystore-password&quot;, &quot;key-manager-password&quot;, &quot;trust-store-password&quot;, &quot;truststore-password&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(keystore-password|key-manager-password|trust-?store-password)[=:\s]\s*\S+&#x27;

  # ===========================================================================
  # BROAD GENERIC CATCH-ALL (noisier by design — catches the patterns above
  # regardless of which service/keyword surrounds them). Expect false positives;
  # delete this block if the report gets too noisy and rely on the specific rules.
  # ===========================================================================
  - id: infra-generic-keyname-secret
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Any key named *password/secret/token/credential/apikey = value
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;password&quot;, &quot;passwd&quot;, &quot;pwd&quot;, &quot;passphrase&quot;, &quot;secret&quot;, &quot;token&quot;, &quot;apikey&quot;, &quot;api_key&quot;, &quot;credential&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)[a-z0-9_.\-]*(password|passwd|pwd|passphrase|secret|token|api[_-]?key|credential)s?\s*[:=&gt;]+\s*[&quot;\x27]?[^\s&quot;\x27]+&#x27;

  - id: infra-generic-cli-password-flag
    category: InfraCreds
    title: Any --password/--pass/--pw CLI flag with inline value
    severity: HIGH
    keywords: [&quot;--password&quot;, &quot;--passwd&quot;, &quot;--pass&quot;, &quot;--pw&quot;]
    regex: &#x27;(?i)(--password|--passwd|--pass|--pw)[=\s]\s*\S+&#x27;</code></pre>

<h2>PII rules used (trivy-pii.yaml)</h2>
<pre class="yaml"><code># trivy-pii.yaml — biometric + biographic PII.
# Use: trivy fs --scanners secret --secret-config trivy-pii.yaml &lt;path&gt;

allow-rules:
